# Absolute rules

Time is an integer tick. One tick is 1.25 ns. Do not store or add a floating-point nanosecond value.

`delay(k)` is a FIFO of length k. `push` returns the value inserted k ticks earlier. Do not schedule with `readyAt = t + k`.

```typescript
// BAD: overlap cannot emerge
const readyAt = tick + colAccess

// GOOD: shift a k-deep register every device tick
const { fifo, out } = pushDelay(column, token)
```

Gates, decoders, and muxes are pure. No closed-over state. Thread bank FSMs and queues as fields.

One DRAM core, three interface wrappers. Do not copy the bank state machine per architecture.

Each device steps only when its own divider edge fires. SDR steps the core every 8 ticks, not every tick.

Workload randomness takes a seed. Do not call `Math.random`.

A timer decrements on each device tick. The state changes on the tick the timer becomes 0.

```typescript
// BAD: transitions one tick late
if (bank.timer === 0) bank.state = 'active'
else bank.timer -= 1

// GOOD
const timer = bank.timer - 1
if (timer === 0) return complete(bank)
return { ...bank, timer }
```
